    <p class="section-id">BACKGROUND <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> ENGINEERING PRACTICE</p>
    <h1>Engineering<br /><span class="accent">with context.</span></h1>
    <p class="inner-lead">My foundation is more than eight years working across data engineering, cloud platforms and analytics. My current direction adds AI product development and user-facing solution delivery.</p>
  </div></section>
  <div class="shell experience-grid">
    <article class="experience-panel"><p class="section-id">01 / FOUNDATIONS</p><h2>Data platforms</h2><p>Data engineering, distributed processing, lakehouse architectures and integration work. Core technologies include <strong>Azure, Databricks, Spark/PySpark and Delta Lake</strong>, with practical attention to governance, security, CI/CD and system reliability.</p></article>
    <article class="experience-panel"><p class="section-id">02 / PRODUCT DELIVERY</p><h2>Applied AI & full stack</h2><p>Beyond platform foundations, I explore usable product workflows that combine <strong>APIs, interfaces, AI-assisted extraction, external services and asynchronous processing</strong>. My case studies show design choices and verification gaps without disclosing private application code.</p></article>
    <article class="experience-panel"><p class="section-id">03 / TECHNICAL APPROACH</p><h2>From ambiguity to evidence</h2><ul><li>Discover the actual user problem and operating constraints.</li><li>Design data and model boundaries with explicit trade-offs.</li><li>Test assumptions with reproducible evidence.</li><li>Deliver usable systems and learn from operational behavior.</li></ul></article>
    <article class="experience-panel"><p class="section-id">04 / DIRECTION</p><h2>Forward Deployed Engineering</h2><p>I'm building toward work that combines <strong>customer discovery, software engineering, data/AI integration and measured outcomes</strong>. The public lab roadmap sets out the engineering proof I want to make reproducible.</p><a href="/roadmap/" class="text-link" style="margin-top:25px">Explore planned labs ↗</a></article>
  </div>
